{#
   SCE Protocol-Synthesis RFC §synth-5-O — per-backend SCE-MAP marker macros.

   Spec lines 3094-3160 fix the marker syntax per backend:
     - C  / Cpp:   `#line {line} "{file}"` (preprocessor directive)
     - Rust:       BOTH `#[doc = "SCE-MAP: …"]` AND `// SCE-MAP: …`
                   per spec lines 3135-3136 "MUST emit BOTH" — an
                   empirical preservation test asserts that rustdoc
                   keeps the `#[doc]` form on every emitted function.
     - Kotlin:     `// SCE-MAP: {file}:{line}`
     - Go:         `//line {file}:{line}` (recognised by `go vet` +
                                           panic stack traces)
     - Python:     `# SCE-MAP: {file}:{line}`

   `loc` is the IR-attached `Option<SourceLocation>` populated by the
   parser at every emission-eligible node (SCE Protocol-Synthesis RFC §synth-5-O;
   see `sce-build/src/forge/provenance.rs`). The macro
   silently elides when `loc` is None — the codegen pre-emit walker
   (`validate_emission_provenance`) already gates on the populate, so
   a None reaching this point is a parser-site regression caught by
   the `traceability/scxml-line-range-missing` diagnostic, not a
   silent miss [[feedback-silently-broken-hooks]].

   `module_level=true` switches the Rust emission to the inner-attribute
   form `#![doc = "..."]` so a top-of-module marker doesn't collide with
   a `pub` item's own rustdoc. Other backends ignore the flag.

   The macro is invoked once per backend at the top of the generated
   state machine source (proving the infrastructure end-to-end) and
   again at per-state on_entry/on_exit + per-transition handlers +
   forge per-kind body functions; the macro is single-source-of-truth
   so a syntax tweak there edits one place.

   `symbol_state` + `symbol_artifact` carry the marked symbol's
   identity. Spec lines 3117 / 3153 / 3158 fix the comment-form marker
   as `SCE-MAP: <scxml_file>:<line> :: <state> :: <artifact>` — the
   two segments are exactly the identity half of the mangled symbol
   (`forge::symbol_mangling::mangle`), so a consumer holding only the
   source listing can rebuild the sidecar key without re-walking the
   IR. Document-root symbols (`_machine`, `_forge_body`) have no state
   path; they render the artifact alone (` :: <artifact>`), the
   artifact staying the last ` :: ` field either way so the parse rule
   is one rule.

   The values are NEVER spelled as literals at a call site: constants
   come from the `sce_artifact` global (registered in
   `generator::new_env` off the `ARTIFACT_*` consts) and per-transition
   labels ride home on the transition itself
   (`symbol_state_path` / `symbol_artifact`, stamped by
   `symbol_mangling::stamp_symbol_attribution`). A template that
   derived the identity from its render site would be wrong wherever a
   backend renders inherited transitions under a descendant's arm.

   `line` is a single line, not a range: `SourceLocation` records one
   line per node, which is the same reason the sidecar's `line_range`
   is `[n, n]`. A range shape belongs to the round that gives the
   parser spans, together with its producer.

   The per-symbol attribution is also emitted as JSON sidecar
   (`out/{language}/sce_sourcemap.json`); the in-source markers are
   the line-resolution fallback when only the source listing is
   available (e.g. JTAG hard-fault stack trace, panic backtrace).
#}

{#
   `stmt_level=true` marks an emission site inside a function body —
   a `match` arm, a `switch` case — rather than above an item. Rust is
   the only backend that has to care: `#[doc = "..."]` is an item
   attribute and does not parse in expression position, so the
   statement form emits the `//` comment alone. Every other backend
   emits exactly what it emits at function scope, because `#line`,
   `//line` and comments are all valid mid-body.

   Statement-level markers are what make the per-symbol attribution
   real. A marker above `execute_entry_actions` can only name one
   location for a function every state shares, which is why every
   committed tree carried a single distinct marker value per file
   until the call sites started passing the state's own location.
#}
{%- macro source_marker(loc, backend, module_level=false, symbol_state="", symbol_artifact="", stmt_level=false) -%}
{%- if loc and loc.line -%}
{%- set range_part = loc.line -%}
{#- Attribution suffix per spec lines 3117/3153/3158. The artifact is
    always the trailing ` :: ` field; the state field precedes it only
    when the symbol has a state path. `#line` / `//line` directives
    take no suffix — their syntax is fixed by the language and the
    attribution reaches the consumer through DWARF instead. -#}
{%- set state_part = " :: " ~ symbol_state if symbol_state else "" -%}
{%- set sym_suffix = state_part ~ " :: " ~ symbol_artifact if symbol_artifact else "" -%}
{%- if backend == "c" or backend == "cpp" -%}
{#- C/Cpp `#line` is a preprocessor directive that remaps line
    numbers for the *rest of the translation unit*. At file scope
    (especially in a `.h` header included by many TUs) this would
    propagate into every consumer's diagnostics. The comment form
    is safe at module scope; per-function emission switches to
    `#line`, where the redirect is locally scoped to the function
    body. -#}
{%- if module_level %}
// SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}
{%- else %}
#line {{ loc.line }} "{{ loc.file }}"
{%- endif %}
{%- elif backend == "rust" -%}
{%- if module_level %}
#![doc = "SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}"]
// SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}
{%- elif stmt_level %}
// SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}
{%- else %}
#[doc = "SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}"]
// SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}
{%- endif %}
{%- elif backend == "kotlin" %}
// SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}
{%- elif backend == "go" -%}
{#- Go's `//line` directive remaps subsequent line numbers in panic
    stack traces + `go vet` output. Like C/Cpp `#line`, file-scope
    placement would shift every subsequent file position. Use the
    comment form at module level; per-function emission switches
    to `//line`. -#}
{%- if module_level %}
// SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}
{%- else %}
//line {{ loc.file }}:{{ loc.line }}
{%- endif %}
{%- elif backend == "python" %}
# SCE-MAP: {{ loc.file }}:{{ range_part }}{{ sym_suffix }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
